      <p>At the top of Settings, a strip shows the palette a step at a time. <strong>Uniform</strong> is the evenly spaced lineup. <strong>Turned</strong> is the same lineup turned around the circle to best match the placed hues; turning keeps it uniform. <strong>+H</strong> adds the placed hues, and <strong>+M</strong> colorfulness per hue. How far the edits take the palette from the turned lineup is its <strong>bend</strong>, in gaps: one gap is the even difference between neighbors${l?`, ${l.toFixed(1)} \u0394E in ${t.mode} mode here`:""}, \u0394E being how different two colors look in CAM16-UCS. Here's the strip for this palette; point at a swatch or a row for its numbers, and click a number for what it means.</p>
